  - [ ] elite bosses should use all weapons the player can use, depending on situation (e.g: dont launch a rocket if not safe, use shotgun or flamethrower depending on distance etc)) — investigated (2026-07-16, no code changed yet); depends on the boss item above existing first.
    - **No enemy weapon-variety system exists at all today.** Every ranged enemy attack, elite or not, is one fixed generic bolt: `enemyAi.ts` calls `spawnProjectile` unconditionally, one shot, no weapon concept. The player's real variety (`weapons.ts`) boils down to two actual mechanisms under the hood, not six: hitscan pellets (parameterized by `pellets` count + cone + damage — pistol/shotgun/gdb/Friday Hotfix are all this, just different numbers) and `isRocket` (Ghidra only, the real `spawnRocket` physical-projectile path, `rockets.ts`). Reusing "shotgun vs flamethrower" for a boss is comparatively cheap (loop `spawnProjectile` N times with angle variance instead of once); reusing rockets is not — enemies have never fired one, and `rockets.ts`'s `updateRockets` only currently checks for hitting *enemies*, not the player, so an enemy-fired rocket needs a new detonate-against-player interaction, not just a new call site.
    - **The "situational" logic this asks for already exists, but only outside the real game** — `scripts/run-balancing-telemetry.mjs`'s `pickRangedWeapon`/`rocketAimUnsafe` (this session's own work: close-cluster vs distant-cluster weapon choice, the multi-iteration rocket-vs-mine safety fix) is proven, working logic for exactly this situational pattern. It is **not** reusable code, though — it's Node-side bot-script logic driving the page via keyboard events, structurally separate from `enemyAi.ts`'s real in-engine AI. The *design* (distance-gated weapon choice, a safe-rocket-distance check) is a good reference to port the idea from, not a function to import.
    - Real scope if picked up: per-boss weapon-choice logic in `enemyAi.ts` (distance/cluster-aware, mirroring the bot's proven distance thresholds conceptually), a multi-pellet firing loop for the hitscan-style attacks, and the new enemy-fires-rocket-at-player interaction in `rockets.ts`. Depends on the boss tier itself existing (the item above) — no boss to attach this behavior to otherwise.
